  "research": {
    "area-3": {
      "text": "Why scout here\nThis area, near Don Mills Road and Lawrence Avenue East, offers a commercial environment that could suit a new café with an indoor playground. The CF Shops at Don Mills is a prominent lifestyle center with a variety of retail stores, restaurants, and entertainment options. This suggests a consistent flow of visitors to the immediate vicinity. The presence of other food and drink establishments, including cafes like CoCo and Pablo's Coffee House, indicates an existing market for café services. The area is described as integrating office, retail, dining, and entertainment uses in a walkable urban setting, which could provide a diverse customer base.\n\nReasons to hesitate\nThe specific zoning for a café with an indoor playground needs careful investigation. While general retail and cafes are permitted in commercial zones, an indoor playground component could introduce additional requirements. Toronto's zoning by-laws for \"eating establishments\" and \"amusement establishments\" need to be reviewed to determine if they cover this hybrid concept. Changes to zoning by-laws in Toronto are allowing more small-scale retail and cafes in neighborhoods, but there are criteria related to lot type and proximity to schools, parks, or commercial sites, which would need to be checked against a specific property. It's crucial to understand that an existing commercial use for a unit does not automatically permit an indoor playground.\n\nNearby concepts and menu checks\nThe CF Shops at Don Mills hosts various food and drink establishments. These include Kitaya Japanese Takeout, Asian Legend, Sorento Italian Kitchen, Diwan at the Aga Khan Museum, and Eataly. Eataly offers a diverse range of Italian classics, including grab-and-go options and seated restaurants. Other cafes like CoCo are also present. To understand pricing and offerings, official menus for these specific establishments within the CF Shops at Don Mills would need to be reviewed, as online aggregators may not reflect current pricing or full menus.\n\nAccess and local context\nThe area around Don Mills Road and Lawrence Avenue East is well-connected, with close proximity to the Don Valley Parkway (DVP) and surface public transit routes. The CF Shops at Don Mills itself provides on-site parking along internal streets, in surface lots, and within a multi-level parkade. This accessibility is beneficial for attracting customers. The lifestyle center also includes amenities like family washrooms and nursing rooms, which could be relevant for a café targeting families.\n\nWhat to check on a visit\nA site visit should confirm the specific zoning designation of any potential property and inquire with the City of Toronto Planning Division about regulations for a café combined with an indoor playground. Questions regarding permits required for an \"amusement establishment\" or a \"place of assembly\" should be addressed, as these may apply to an indoor playground. It would be important to assess the available interior space for both the café seating and the playground area, ensuring it meets any size or layout requirements. Enquire about the process for obtaining building permits and occupancy reviews for a change of use or new construction related to an indoor playground. Additionally, research any specific fire safety regulations and capacity limits for venues with indoor play structures. The potential for outdoor patio space, and its associated permitting, should also be investigated.",
